WEBVTT

00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:11.679
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twentieth of April. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:12.109 --> 00:00:17.359
<v Hannah Price>We can hear you. Anyone see the football last night? Honestly, that last ten minutes.</v>

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.199
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, unfortunately. I'd nearly recovered until you mentioned it.</v>

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:29.940
<v Grace Liu>I avoided it. Our weekend plans were a walk and a pub lunch, but the weather put paid to the walk.</v>

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:34.880
<v Jamie Brennan>So just the pub lunch, then. Terrible outcome.</v>

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.490
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Next weekend we're planning the garden, weather permitting. Which probably means another pub lunch.</v>

00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:47.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the leisure committee. Anything finished that we can get off the board?</v>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.079
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, finished the repair on the line 3 chiller last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.929
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Closed, not another job for this shift.</v>

00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:04.030
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I tested the Gas Turbine 1 yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.859
<v Marcus Hale>That's the one I saw marked complete, yeah?</v>

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:12.829
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, same one. Finished, no outstanding bit hidden underneath it.</v>

00:01:13.189 --> 00:01:18.790
<v Hannah Price>I already swapped the filter on the line 1 mould temp yesterday as well. That's complete.</v>

00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:22.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, cheers. Anything from nights that's just information?</v>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:31.159
<v Hannah Price>Noticed the wrapper was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down. Just an observation, not raising a job.</v>

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:35.239
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, understood. Not something still sitting there hot.</v>

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:45.640
<v Jamie Brennan>Similar sort of thing: saw the pressure on the Compressed Air Dryer dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own. Just passing that on.</v>

00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:50.859
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, heard. A dip that recovered, not a new fault-finding job from this meeting.</v>

00:01:52.319 --> 00:01:59.670
<v Sarah Okafor>And we're still waiting on parts for the line three. Nothing we can do until they arrive, so that remains blocked.</v>

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:05.760
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, that one's parked. Separate from the chiller repair I've finished.</v>

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:14.340
<v Grace Liu>Also, the shutdown on the outfeed conveyor is cancelled now. Production need it running, so that shutdown isn't happening.</v>

00:02:15.139 --> 00:02:20.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, cancelled, not postponed onto somebody's list today. Let's get the actual commitments straight.</v>

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:26.020
<v Grace Liu>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the IM2 this morning.</v>

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. The IM2 risk assessment, this morning.</v>

00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:33.090
<v Grace Liu>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:40.340
<v Sarah Okafor>We've also got the seals on the MV01 needing replacement. Who's taking that one?</v>

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:49.020
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll replace the seals on the MV01 next week. Drop everything for that one, yeah — that's the priority I'll give it.</v>

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.750
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, talking over you. Next week still, rather than bringing it forward?</v>

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:02.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Next week, definitely. High urgency when we do it, not changing it to today.</v>

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:09.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Jamie Brennan has the MV01 seals next week. Drop everything for that one. Clear.</v>

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:15.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, if you've got a spare minute, can you send the shift handover report round?</v>

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.400
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. It's a spare-minute one, no need to bump anything else for it.</v>

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:35.569
<v Hannah Price>I'll go to Tollgate Water Treatment Works to pick up the replacement parts for the cooling tower tomorrow.</v>

00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:40.110
<v Jamie Brennan>Tomorrow for the collection, yeah? Sorry, your sound clipped at the end.</v>

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:46.789
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, tomorrow. And drop everything for that one — I'll treat that collection as the priority.</v>

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:53.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Tollgate Water Treatment Works, replacement parts for the cooling tower, tomorrow. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:00.810
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I'll do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:06.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, that's on the 3rd, with the contractor at the warehouse?</v>

00:04:08.539 --> 00:04:11.689
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's right, on the 3rd. I'll do that visit.</v>

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:19.209
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tomasz Nowak, can you chase the purchase order for the Compressed Air Dryer by 11am?</v>

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.209
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yes, I'll chase the purchase order for the Compressed Air Dryer by 11am.</v>

00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:32.100
<v Jamie Brennan>Just to keep those separate, that's the purchase order chase. My pressure comment earlier was only something I saw.</v>

00:04:33.149 --> 00:04:37.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. The purchase order is the action, the pressure dip was information.</v>

00:04:38.439 --> 00:04:42.990
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll take vibration readings on the number two bearing on Friday. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Olu, number two bearing readings on Friday, normal priority.</v>

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep. I'll take those, no rush-job label on that one.</v>

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.350
<v Marcus Hale>Normal priority. Nice to hear those words together for once.</v>

00:04:59.949 --> 00:05:05.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't get too comfortable. Grace Liu, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team?</v>

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:14.850
<v Grace Liu>I can't take that one, sorry. I've got the IM2 risk assessment this morning, and I haven't got the capacity to organise the talk as well.</v>

00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:20.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Jamie, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team instead?</v>

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.540
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team. That's with me instead.</v>

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:35.029
<v Grace Liu>Thanks. Definitely handed over, then, rather than both of us thinking the other one's got it.</v>

00:05:37.399 --> 00:05:39.850
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, mine. Teams has witnesses and everything.</v>

00:05:41.389 --> 00:05:48.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And the two drop-everything jobs keep the dates we've said. Urgent doesn't mean we've quietly moved them into this morning.</v>

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:55.560
<v Marcus Hale>Makes sense. Otherwise everything ends up in the same red box and the box stops meaning anything.</v>

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:04.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Line three stays blocked on parts, and the outfeed conveyor shutdown is cancelled. Neither is a new action.</v>

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:11.300
<v Grace Liu>All clear from me. At least this plan's firmer than my weekend weather forecast.</v>

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.689
<v Hannah Price>And less depressing than the football, hopefully.</v>

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:18.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Low bar. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
